  id: Right_Aortic_Arch2
  partName: Right Aortic Arch
  descriptionChunks:
  - A secondary right aortic arch variant refers to an additional or anomalous vascular
    structure that branches from the right side of the aortic system. This structure
    may contribute to vascular ring formation or represent a distinct anatomical
    segment within the cardiac outflow tract.
  - Its presence can impact blood distribution and may be associated with congenital
    cardiovascular anomalies. Identifying and understanding such variants is important
    for accurate anatomical mapping, surgical planning, and veterinary diagnosis
    of complex heart and great vessel conditions.
